// Exclusive aggregate values (docs/semantics/27_ownership_clean.md section
// 2.3 step 7, for the storage the collection verdict tracks). A value is
// exclusive when no other live value names an Array buffer it reaches. Only
// such a buffer may grow through a member alias, because growth frees the
// old buffer every other copy still names.
//
// - An array literal, a Clone and a MapKeys result are fresh.
// - A constructor is exclusive when every tracked argument is exclusive,
//   consumed, and distinct from the other arguments.
// - A user call is exclusive when its routine's result is, and the argument
//   of each formal that flows into that result is exclusive and consumed.
// - A local is exclusive when every definition is (a greatest fixed point,
//   so `x = F(x)` threading keeps it), and a member path when its root is.
// - A default or inout formal is exclusive under its callers' obligation; the
//   classification records it as a dependency. An own formal is exclusive.
// - An indexed read, a ref formal and anything else may be shared.

import "ast_collection_exclusive_whole_carried_field_owner.pgy";
import "ast_collection_exclusive_value_classification_owner.pgy";
import "ast_collection_exclusive_value_fact_build_owner.pgy";
